  "worked_solution": "The set $N$ denotes the set of all natural numbers. It is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\nN={1,2,3,\u2026}={Z}^{+}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${Z}^{+}.$\n\nThe other options are *not* equivalent to $N:$\n\n- The set ${N}_{0}$ includes the element zero, and $0\\notin N.$\n\n- The set $Z$ includes all the negative integers, and $-1\\notin N,-2\\notin N,\u2026\\,.$\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ is the set of positive rational numbers, and ${Q}^{+}\\ne N.$\n\n- The set ${1,2,4,8,16,\u2026}$ does not include the elements $3,5\u2026$ and $3\\in N,$ $5\\in N,\u2026\\,.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
